    {
      "review_id": "ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNZbzd1R1VREAE",
      "author": "siva p",
      "rating": 1,
      "relative_date": "7 years ago",
      "text": "We have had two bad experiences with Dr. Mustafa. He is very casual in his diagnosis, and you are just another customer to him. In the first instance, after ruling out chest infection, he was about to dismiss us and we had to really coax him to make examine my mother more. Upon such insistence he identified the onset of cellulitis. Instead of educating us the importance of following up on that condition, he casually mentioned that we might want to see another general practitioner. It could have been fatal, has we not, by stroke of luck followed up. In the second instance, we got an x-ray done, as per his recommendation which actually was the right recommendation. But instead of probing the x-ray in depth and identify the onset of another serious condition, he was very casual in his examination, which turned to be very traumatic to us. I will avoid the details. But suffice to say that Dr. Mustafa should take interest in patient and have a desire to heal patients rather than seeing them as customers. His bedside manners also leave much to be desired. Hope he gets to see this review and improve his functioning. I am appalled to see the other two positive reviews which seem to have been ghost scripted by himself.",
